INT. PLANETARIUM - DOME - NIGHT

A star field wheels overhead. Under it, rows of reclining seats. In the center aisle, a body lies sprawled beneath a projector.

CHIEF SALMA RAHIMI (50s, rain jacket) crouches by the dead man. DEPUTY TOBIAS FINCH (20s, notebook) stands at her shoulder. DR. BRANDT (60s, the planetarium director, trembling) hugs a laser pointer. OYELARAN (40s, night janitor, mop bucket) hovers. SUNNY (30s, ticket clerk, headset around her neck) bites her thumbnail.

RAHIMI
Nobody leaves the dome.

FINCH
Chief, the exits are sealed.

RAHIMI
Then nobody breathes loudly.

Brandt lets out a nervous laugh. Oyelaran shifts his mop.

OYELARAN
(muttering)
I mopped this floor at ten. There were no footprints.

RAHIMI
Say that again.

OYELARAN
No footprints, ma'am. Ten o'clock.

Rahimi looks at the carpet. Muddy prints, wet and fresh, lead from the body to Sunny's seat. Sunny sees them. Freezes.

SUNNY
Those aren't mine.

FINCH
Miss, your boots.

SUNNY
They're not mine!

RAHIMI
(to the room)
Everyone. Show me your shoes.

Nobody moves. Above them, a comet slides across the dome.

BRANDT
(to himself)
Oh god. Oh god. Not the telescope.
